               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="11XX" notBefore="1100" notAfter="1199" calendar="#gregorian">s. xii</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e" source="3701"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_316">Lincoln, Lincolnshire.
                        Cathedral church of St Mary the Virgin</orgName><p>"Liber sancte marie
                        [...]". The erased name begins either "hu" or "lin", followed by one or two
                        letters with a curly vertical mark of abbreviation above the last.
                        Inscription of s. xii ex. or xiii in. (?), on a specially ruled pencil line
                        with title "glosatura porretani super psalterium" immediately
                        below.</p><p>The regular form of inscription in Lincoln books of s. xii is
                        "liber sancte marie linc'" on a ruled pencil line, with title and later
                        pricemark below: this MS. was evidently removed from Lincoln before the
                        pricemarks were inserted in the Lincoln books.</p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cf. old cat. 60</note></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Given to Balliol by Bishop William
                     Gray.</provenance>
               <provenance source="7680"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire. Balliol
                        College (Domus de Balliolo)</orgName><p>‘From Lincoln cathedral priory: on
                        1v (fly-leaf) is a large erased inscription Liber sc?e marie Linc’, with an
                        early title Glosatura Porretani super Psalterium. It is almost certainly the
                        volume entered in the 12th-cent. Lincoln booklist as the gift of Bishop
                        Robert de Chesney, who died in December 1166’ (Mynors, Balliol, 26)‘Liber
                        domus de Balliolo in Oxon’ | ex dono Willemi [sic in Mynors] Gray Eliensis
                        episcopi’ (fol. 1v)</p><p>SC ---- 65 [as-yet unpr. Lincoln booklist, c.
                        1170]Not UO21.1, as (erroneosly) identified there; that is Pauline epistles,
                        not Psalms</p><p>See also under LINCOLN, Lincolnshire, Cathedral church of
                        St Mary the Virgin</p></provenance>
                  </history>
